      "description": "Watch Aberdeen vs Heart Of Midlothian highlights and goals from Premiership - Scotland on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 1, 2026. The stage was set for a classic Scottish Premiership encounter on August 1, 2026 , as Aberdeen welcomed Heart of Midlothian . Both sides brought a high level of intensity to the pitch, knowing that every point in this early-season clash would be vital. Hearts Take the Initiative Heart of Midlothian started the match with a clear tactical plan, looking to disrupt Aberdeen ’s rhythm with a physical approach. The competitive nature of the game was evident early on when Brad Lyons received a yellow card in the 34th minute. The visitors capitalized on their momentum just a minute later, as Oisin McEntee found the back of the net to give the visitors a deserved lead. Aberdeen struggled to find an immediate response, and despite Jordi Altena picking up a caution for the visitors shortly before the break, Hearts headed into the interval with their noses in front. Tactical Adjustments and Rising Tension As the second half got underway, the match evolved into a game of chess between the two managers. A flurry of substitutions followed after the hour mark, with players like Stuart Armstrong , Gavin Molloy , and Jamie McCart introduced to alter the dynamic. Aberdeen gradually began to dominate possession, piling pressure on the visitors' backline. The tension reached a boiling point as the match entered its final phase, with Harry Milne receiving a yellow card in the 89th minute as Hearts fought desperately to protect their slender advantage. The Ultimate Stoppage-Time Turnaround Just as the clock hit the 90-minute mark, the match exploded into life. Kevin Nisbet leveled the scores after being set up by Lewis Mayo , sending the home crowd into a frenzy. The drama intensified in the 93rd minute when Stuart Findlay was shown a straight red card, leading to furious protests from the visiting side. Capitalizing on the chaos, Aberdeen were awarded a penalty in the 95th minute. Kevin Nisbet stepped up to calmly slot home his second of the game, completing a stunning turnaround. Despite a late yellow card for Nisbet during the celebrations, Aberdeen held firm through eleven minutes of stoppage time to claim all three points."
